  {
   "type": "Intro",
   "props": {
    "id": "Intro-3",
    "band": "top",
    "blocks": [
     {
      "type": "Heading",
      "props": {
       "id": "Heading-1",
       "eyebrow": "Run of show",
       "slab": true,
       "title": "Three run of show templates, already timed.",
       "titleTag": "h1",
       "titleClass": "h2 display",
       "lede": "Most run-of-show documents carry the band as one row that says <em>band plays</em>, and the detail gets filled in during the week of the event, by email, at speed. Here's that detail already worked out for the three kinds of night we see most. Take them, change the times, delete what doesn't apply."
      }
     }
    ],
    "_notes": "Run of show templates. The most useful thing on the site for a planner\n     who has not hired us: it is work they have to do anyway, done. The band\n     rows are the ones normally left as \"band plays\" until the week of.",
    "_file": "01-intro.html"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "Text",
   "props": {
    "id": "Text-8",
    "band": "sunk",
    "blocks": [
     {
      "type": "Title",
      "props": {
       "id": "Title-4",
       "html": "How to read these",
       "tag": "h2",
       "cls": "h3"
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "Paragraph",
      "props": {
       "id": "Paragraph-5",
       "html": "The <strong>cue</strong> column is the one worth settling before the day. Every moment in an evening belongs to somebody, and what usually goes wrong is two people each assuming the other was going to nod at the band, or nobody knowing who decides the speeches are running long.",
       "cls": "prose"
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "Paragraph",
      "props": {
       "id": "Paragraph-6",
       "html": "Agree the cue column at sound check with the person holding the master document. Our bandleader takes their cues from that one person.",
       "cls": "prose"
      }
     }
    ],
    "_file": "01-intro.html"
   }
  },
